Abstract:
This paper introduces the idea of Indoor Navigation using Augmented Reality, we propose a QR code location position system using the augmented reality technique for indoor navigation. This system advice directions to the destination in the user's camera screen. QR codes will be installed at some locations in the building assuming any destination can be the starting point of the user. Users can scan a QR code to choose a destination. AR foundation takes live feed from the user's camera and does simultaneous localization and mapping to update the user's location. We use the A * algorithm to find the shortest path to the chosen destination and the directions to the destination are shown in user's camera screen by using some essential plugins like AR foundation. We point to developing the way between the start point location and end point in the simplest way possible so that the users can easily reach their destination by just opening the camera where the directions are shown as animations in their surroundings. We also can add some animate models so that we can see in real world, which help users feel more interactive and immersive.
