Introduction

With the need of human development, the outdoor navigation is developed firstly, when people traveling or drive the car from one place to another, for outdoor navigation, the GPS is enough to meet the people's needs. However, with the increasing development of technology, the building be built very complex, such as airport, the shopping mail, hospital and so on. Therefore, a good indoor navigate application is very useful for people's life. [1]

Indoor navigation deals with navigation within buildings. Because GPS reception is normally nonexistent inside building, Wi-Fi or Bluetooth Beacons may be useful for indoor environment, but both are not providing accurate data to help make sure the right positions. [2] There has an accuracy of nearly 15 meters and require costly hardware installation. However, it is easily can see your surroundings. Therefore, we intend to develop an indoor navigation application using augmented reality.

Our system has several distinct advantages over all other location positioning systems. First, it is an economical solution because the marker that identifies each location is a simply printed on paper, and the mobile PC and camera are general devices that can be implemented in software. Second, although our system has inferior performance than other systems such as GPS or sensor-based location positioning systems, it is not limited by signal propagation and multiple reflections. To increase performance, it adapts via an adaptive thresholding method to detect markers under illumination changes, and it uses the location model to reduce execution time during QR code matching.

In this paper, we propose an application can capture the environment image, and get the data transfer to application, which we can get the accurate position and shows the shortest the destination between right now location to the end point by using augment reality, the navigation line will be showing in user's screen. This paper proposes an augmented reality app for smartphone that navigates a user to a desired area on the augmented reality frame-work AR foundation and ZXing, which help users feel more interactive and immersive. [3]

In following paper, we will show the configuration of indoor navigation system. Describe every parts function. And generate the android app by unity test in real environment. These systems imitate is need serval QR maker install in environment, in the future research, we also continue use the camera to capture the image, but it is no need install any makers, the camera capture the environment image sent to our image algorithm to realize and calculate the real location points, in which we can know the shortest line between the user's location and destination.
SECTION 1
Indoor Navigation System Framework and Description
1.1 Framework

Our indoor navigation system consist of four parts, before the work starting, we need make sure the area where provide the space to navigate, and we can need build the real environment's model, there are two methods be provided, building the model by software, or scanning by laser, if you want to get more accurate model, using the 3dmax remodel is necessary. in this step, we need make sure the model coordinate is same as the real environment's coordinate, because we will augment the virtual things shown in real world. [4]

Then, import the model to unity and set up the AR foundation environment, adding the AR camera and AR session in scene, under the AR camera, we can see the real world and virtual things at the same time. Using the A * algorithm to find the shortest line between the start location and target location.

After finish make up the virtual things, we generate the android application in unity platform, and put it in mobile phone, when user open our application in mobile phone, our application will use the camera to capture the environment information such as QR code, after identify the code, the user's location will update, chose the target location, the augmented navigate line will show in user's phone, which will lead users to the destination by using augmented reality.
