2.3 A* Algorithm

A* is an informed search algorithm, that is formulated in terms of weighted graphs: starting from a specific starting node of a graph, it aims to find a path to the given goal node having the smallest. It does this by maintaining a tree of path originating at the start node and extending those paths one edges at a time until its termination is satisfied.

A * algorithm is one of the best and popular techniques used in pathfinding. At each iteration of its main loop, A * needs to determine which of its paths to extend it. It does so based on the cost if the path and an estimate of the cost required to extend the path all the way to the goal. It simple terms the algorithm can be expressed as: F = G + H (1) View Source Right-click on figure for MathML and additional features. \begin{equation*} F=G+H\tag{1}\end{equation*} Where, F is the parameter which is the sum of the other parameter G and H and is the least cost from one node to the next node. This parameter is responsible for helping us find the most optimal path from our source to destination.
2.4 Qr Code Maker

The process detects a QR code from an input image, we use the online QR code generator and create the four targets which is corresponding with the destination targets. When user use their mobile camera point the QR code, which is a 20*20cm marker, the code text will be sent to unity, and we use the ZXing tool which is specially for decode the QR code. The QR code text is same as the target's object name, when the text is matching, the target position will be update in application, the user's location will update same as QR code which they scan. [7]

