SECTION 4
Conclusion

Although our system is better than national system, in the previous we has mentioned this system do not build other auxiliary hard base station to help user location, we use the image matching, just need set up some QR code in each location, the camera capture the code and transform the position location to system, which help user know where are they and navigation them to the target location, under the AR camera, it is really immersive. Augmented reality is a highly immersive technology that allows users to feel like they are experiencing virtual objects in a real physical space. However, our system also has some limitation, first, our location area is not enough, there is impossible to calculate the cumulative error with increasing the route. second, QR code need to install many locations when the area is large, which is not convenient. In future research, we will be using the slam algorithm, we still use the camera capture image, then using the algorithm to realize the real environment to help user know the location.

The result of this study indicates that the scanning the QR code to location with augmented reality based indoor navigation provided a user experience with high usability and deeply immersive. Future studies will focus to improving the accurate of location and do research in algorithm to capture the image to realize the environment. We not only can make our indoor navigate application better, but also can adding some animate just like model or other material shown in real world. Which will increasing immersive, and users also can be interactive with those models.
